exports[`buildSpecMarkdown > renders a deterministic, self-consistent spec 1`] = `
"# Design spec: \`player.ext.critdmg\`

**Status:** proposed
**Type:** \`float\`
**Used by:** extstats / compact / critdmg_label (label)
**Update frequency:** on stat recalculation

## Definition

Extended crit-damage percentage shown in the stats panel.

This variable is referenced by a \`ui_panels\` layout binding but is not yet exposed by the hybrasyl server. Until it ships, Brigid treats the binding as unbound and the control renders static (see docs/ui-panel-layout-format.md).

## Server implementation options

File paths below are relative to \`e:\\Dark Ages Dev\\Repos\\server\\hybrasyl\`.

### Option A — new StatUpdateFlags bit on 0x08

Add the value to the primary stat update packet (0x08) behind a new flag.

- \`Internals\\Enums\\StatUpdateFlags.cs\` — add a new \`[Flags]\` bit.
- \`Objects\\StatInfo.cs\` — add the backing property for \`player.ext.critdmg\`.
- \`Objects\\User.cs\` → \`UpdateAttributes()\` — write the field when the new flag is set.
- \`Networking\\ServerPackets\\\` — serialize the field in the 0x08 packet builder.

### Option B — append f32 to the 0xFF ExtendedStats packet

Extend the existing 0xFF extended-stats block with a trailing \`float\`. Best fit for derived/float combat stats that already travel on 0xFF.

- \`Objects\\StatInfo.cs\` — add the backing property for \`player.ext.critdmg\`.
- \`Objects\\User.cs\` → \`UpdateAttributes()\` — include the field in the 0xFF path.
- \`Networking\\ServerPackets\\\` — append the \`f32\` to the ExtendedStats writer.

### Option C — new opcode + ServerPacket class

Introduce a dedicated opcode. Warranted only when the value has its own cadence or grouping that does not belong on 0x08 / 0xFF.

- \`Internals\\Enums\\\` — register the new opcode.
- \`Networking\\ServerPackets\\\` — add a new \`ServerPacket\` subclass.
- \`Objects\\User.cs\` — emit the packet at the appropriate trigger.

**Recommended:** Option B — append f32 to the 0xFF ExtendedStats packet

## Wire format

- Payload: \`f32\` (little-endian), appended to the chosen packet body.

## Client / Brigid expectations

- \`WorldState\` gains a \`float\` property that mirrors \`player.ext.critdmg\`, updated when the packet arrives.
- Raise the matching \`Changed\` event on update so bound controls refresh.
- On the layout side, a bound \`label\`/\`progressbar\` renders the numeric value (with optional \`format\`).

## Binding usage

\`\`\`xml
<label name="my_label" rect="0,0,80,14" bind="player.ext.critdmg" format="{value:0.0}"/>
\`\`\`
"
`;
